  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s0",
      "title": "The question",
      "narration": "In **ΔPQR**, **PQ = 33 cm** and **∠R = 90°**. **H** lies on **PR** such that **PH = 6 cm** and **K** lies on **QR** such that **KR = 13 cm**. Given that **KH = 19 cm**, we have to find (i) **HR** and (ii) **QK**.",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "title": "Spot the right angle",
      "narration": "In ΔKRH, **∠R = 90°**, so the **hypotenuse** is the side opposite it: **KH**. The other two sides meet at the right angle. (∠R is the same angle in ΔPQR and ΔKRH.)",
      "actions": [
        {
          "pulse": [
            "ra0"
          ],
          "at": 700
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "Pythagoras' theorem",
      "narration": "**Pythagoras' theorem**: the square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{KH^2} &= \\role{legA}{KR^2} + \\role{legB}{HR^2}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Make the unknown the subject",
      "narration": "We want a **shorter side**, so subtract the known square from the hypotenuse square.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{KH^2} &= \\role{legA}{KR^2} + \\role{legB}{HR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{HR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{KH^2} - \\role{legA}{KR^2}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "title": "Substitute the lengths",
      "narration": "Replace each side by its length.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{KH^2} &= \\role{legA}{KR^2} + \\role{legB}{HR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{HR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{KH^2} - \\role{legA}{KR^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{19^2} - \\role{legA}{13^2}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "title": "Square and subtract",
      "narration": "Square each number, then subtract.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{KH^2} &= \\role{legA}{KR^2} + \\role{legB}{HR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{HR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{KH^2} - \\role{legA}{KR^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{19^2} - \\role{legA}{13^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{361} - \\role{legA}{169} \\\\ &= \\role{legB}{192}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "title": "Square root",
      "narration": "192 is not a perfect square, so use a calculator and round to 3 significant figures.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{KH^2} &= \\role{legA}{KR^2} + \\role{legB}{HR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{HR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{KH^2} - \\role{legA}{KR^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{19^2} - \\role{legA}{13^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{361} - \\role{legA}{169} \\\\ &= \\role{legB}{192} \\\\ \\role{legB}{HR} &= \\sqrt{192} = 8\\sqrt{3} = \\role{ans}{13.9\\ \\text{cm}}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "title": "Find PR",
      "narration": "For the next step keep more digits: **HR = 13.856…** (not the rounded 13.9).\\[\\begin{aligned}PR &= PH + HR \\\\ &= 6 + 13.856 \\\\ &= 19.856\\ \\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "title": "Right angle and theorem",
      "narration": "In ΔPQR, **∠R = 90°**, so the **hypotenuse** is the side opposite it: **PQ**. The other two sides meet at the right angle. **Pythagoras' theorem**: the square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides. We want a shorter side, so subtract.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{PQ^2} &= \\role{legA}{PR^2} + \\role{legB}{QR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{QR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{PQ^2} - \\role{legA}{PR^2}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": [
        {
          "pulse": [
            "ra0"
          ],
          "at": 700
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "title": "Substitute and subtract",
      "narration": "Put in the lengths, square them and subtract.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{PQ^2} &= \\role{legA}{PR^2} + \\role{legB}{QR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{QR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{PQ^2} - \\role{legA}{PR^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{33^2} - \\role{legA}{19.856^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{1089} - \\role{legA}{394.26} \\\\ &= \\role{legB}{694.74}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "title": "Square root",
      "narration": "694.74 is not a perfect square. Use a calculator and keep 4 significant figures — we need this value again.\\[\\begin{aligned}\\role{hyp}{PQ^2} &= \\role{legA}{PR^2} + \\role{legB}{QR^2} \\\\ \\role{legB}{QR^2} &= \\role{hyp}{PQ^2} - \\role{legA}{PR^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{33^2} - \\role{legA}{19.856^2} \\\\ &= \\role{hyp}{1089} - \\role{legA}{394.26} \\\\ &= \\role{legB}{694.74} \\\\ \\role{legB}{QR} &= \\sqrt{694.74} = 26.36\\ \\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "title": "Find QK",
      "narration": "**QK** is the part of **QR** left after taking away **KR**.\\[\\begin{aligned}QK &= QR - KR \\\\ &= 26.36 - 13 \\\\ &= \\role{ans}{13.4\\ \\text{cm}}\\ \\text{(3 s.f.)}\\end{aligned}\\]",
      "actions": []
    }
  ],
  "formulas": [
    {
      "title": "Pythagoras' theorem",
      "tex": "\\role{hyp}{c^2} = \\role{legA}{a^2} + \\role{legB}{b^2}",
      "text": "In a right-angled triangle, the square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides."
    },
    {
      "title": "Finding the hypotenuse",
      "tex": "\\role{hyp}{c} = \\sqrt{\\role{legA}{a^2} + \\role{legB}{b^2}}",
      "text": "Add the two squares, then take the square root."
    },
    {
      "title": "Finding a shorter side",
      "tex": "\\role{legA}{a} = \\sqrt{\\role{hyp}{c^2} - \\role{legB}{b^2}}",
      "text": "Subtract the known shorter side's square from the hypotenuse's square, then take the square root."
    }
  ],
  "challenges": [
